        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <windows>The windows are where the house is loosing the most heat so as an upgrade I replaced any windows that are only double glazed and replaced them with triple glazed, LowE, argon filled units with insulating spacers. These included the skylights, both the sliding glass doors and five other windows. This reduced the heat loss through the windows by 27% or 16 GJ. Replacing them with quadruple glazed windows would reduce that heat loss even more. A number of the windows had air leaking around the frames so replacing them will probably reduce that leakage as well.</windows>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
